WEBVTT

00:01.406 --> 00:04.803
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.804 --> 00:08.178
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.179 --> 00:11.863
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.864 --> 00:14.833
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.834 --> 00:18.303
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.304 --> 00:21.547
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.548 --> 00:23.172
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.173 --> 00:24.809
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.810 --> 00:30.177
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:31.250 --> 00:34.652
<i> Family Guy is filmed
before a live studio audience.</i>

00:36.288 --> 00:37.555
That's Carol,

00:37.556 --> 00:39.491
Lois' sister who was married
to Mayor West,

00:39.492 --> 00:41.993
- but now he's dead.
- I love you, Carol!

00:41.994 --> 00:44.362
We're glad you could come over
for dinner tonight, Carol.

00:44.363 --> 00:46.097
Thank you for having me.

00:46.098 --> 00:48.700
I've been having such a hard
time since Adam passed away.

00:48.701 --> 00:50.802
Aw...

00:50.803 --> 00:53.004
I want to squeeze your butt
and then take your pants down

00:53.005 --> 00:54.406
and look at your butt!

00:54.407 --> 00:55.789
We still can't believe he's gone.

00:55.790 --> 00:59.744
He was such a great mayor,
and a great uncle to the kids.

00:59.745 --> 01:02.213
Wait, Uncle Adam is dead?

01:02.214 --> 01:04.749
Yeesh. How many people
has this show killed?

01:04.750 --> 01:07.052
- Yeah, we're all gonna miss...
- Hey, don't touch me, man!

01:07.053 --> 01:09.320
I'm leaving. I know-I know
what I did. I'm leaving.

01:10.923 --> 01:12.888
Yeah, we're all gonna miss Mayor West.

01:12.889 --> 01:15.857
You know what'll make you
feel better, Aunt Carol?

01:15.858 --> 01:17.462
Doing an Indian guy.

01:17.463 --> 01:19.261
Meg, stop eating with the serving spoon.

01:19.262 --> 01:20.662
Nah.

01:20.663 --> 01:22.998
I just wish there was
some way we could honor

01:22.999 --> 01:25.300
Adam's memory here in town.

01:25.301 --> 01:26.434
You know what we should do?

01:26.435 --> 01:29.134
We should rename the high school
for Mayor West.

01:29.135 --> 01:31.104
What, you mean change it
from James Woods High?

01:31.105 --> 01:33.907
Yeah. James Woods
is an embarrassment to Quahog.

01:33.908 --> 01:36.267
He's a political troll
and a maniac on Twitter.

01:36.268 --> 01:38.211
I think that's a great idea, Brian.

01:38.212 --> 01:39.679
You should meet with Principal Shepherd

01:39.680 --> 01:40.847
and suggest it.

01:40.848 --> 01:42.516
Awesome. And while you do that,

01:42.517 --> 01:45.218
I'll make a special video
dedication reminding people

01:45.219 --> 01:47.554
of how great Mayor West was.

01:49.257 --> 01:51.792
<i>Oceans apart</i>

01:51.793 --> 01:54.594
<i>Day after day</i>

01:55.396 --> 01:59.499
<i>And I slowly go insane</i>

02:00.701 --> 02:02.936
<i>I hear your voice</i>

02:02.937 --> 02:05.672
<i>On the line</i>

02:06.808 --> 02:09.076
<i>But it doesn't stop</i>

02:09.077 --> 02:10.243
<i>The pain</i>

02:11.412 --> 02:12.979
<i>If I see you</i>

02:12.980 --> 02:15.282
<i>Next to never</i>

02:16.417 --> 02:18.185
<i>How can we</i>

02:18.186 --> 02:21.755
<i>Say forever</i>

02:21.756 --> 02:24.591
<i>Wherever you go</i>

02:24.592 --> 02:27.427
<i>Whatever you do</i>

02:27.428 --> 02:29.329
<i>I will be</i>

02:29.330 --> 02:32.966
<i>Right here waiting for you...</i>

02:36.604 --> 02:38.271
So, you'd like to rename the school?

02:38.272 --> 02:39.973
Yes. To Adam West High.

02:39.974 --> 02:42.843
Well, you're a talking dog... you
probably know what you're doing.

02:42.844 --> 02:44.010
Let's do it.

02:44.011 --> 02:46.012
Damn it!

02:46.013 --> 02:48.014
The only thing that's left to do now

02:48.015 --> 02:51.852
is for you to pay the normal
$1,000 principal meeting fee.

02:51.853 --> 02:53.453
What?! Wait a minute.

02:53.454 --> 02:55.522
Do you have a gambling problem?

02:55.523 --> 02:57.724
Me? I don't have a gambling problem.

02:57.725 --> 02:59.926
Points! Just score points!

02:59.927 --> 03:01.928
I don't care who.

03:01.929 --> 03:04.231
Principal Shepherd,
someone named Eddie Payups

03:04.232 --> 03:05.799
is here to see you.

03:05.800 --> 03:07.134
Tell him I need one minute.

03:07.135 --> 03:08.969
Anyway, great idea.
We'll have a ceremony

03:08.970 --> 03:11.004
to change the name
of the school this week.

03:11.005 --> 03:13.140
What's the score of that game right now?

03:13.141 --> 03:15.509
It's, uh, 85-75.

03:15.510 --> 03:17.043
Ugh! Not enough.

03:18.045 --> 03:19.079
Wow, we did it.

03:19.080 --> 03:20.647
We changed the name of the school.

03:20.648 --> 03:22.883
Well, you know, it was
the right thing to do, Brian.

03:22.884 --> 03:26.119
Like when I had to give bad news
to that improv team.

03:26.120 --> 03:29.122
I called you here to tell you
that you're all 45 years old.

03:29.123 --> 03:31.124
Go home and be with your children.

03:36.731 --> 03:38.331
Thank you, everybody, for coming today

03:38.332 --> 03:40.634
as we honor one
of Quahog's finest citizens,

03:40.635 --> 03:42.369
Mayor Adam West.

03:42.370 --> 03:43.670
We will start today's ceremony

03:43.671 --> 03:46.173
with the traditional
21-cat launcher salute

03:46.174 --> 03:48.909
to honor our wacky but beloved mayor.

03:48.910 --> 03:50.410
Ready! Aim!

03:50.411 --> 03:51.578
Meow!

03:52.914 --> 03:55.515
Beautiful. Now, to unveil our new sign,

03:55.516 --> 03:58.518
we've invited HGTV's
Chip and Joanna Gaines,

03:58.519 --> 04:01.555
who are here to prove that their
show didn't ruin their marriage.

04:01.556 --> 04:04.925
All right, Quahog,
are you ready to see your new sign?

04:04.926 --> 04:06.626
Yeah!

04:07.628 --> 04:09.062
Oh, a-are we going that way?

04:09.063 --> 04:12.365
<i>I don't know, Joanna.
What direction are we going?</i>

04:12.366 --> 04:14.334
♪

04:20.341 --> 04:21.408
Uh-oh.

04:21.409 --> 04:23.410
Thank you. Uh, please, uh, stick around

04:23.411 --> 04:25.879
for refreshments and snacks
in the gymnasium.

04:34.522 --> 04:36.656
Go, go, Principal Coffee Breath!

04:39.160 --> 04:41.228
Looking for someone?

04:44.065 --> 04:46.166
I like this episode.

04:49.604 --> 04:52.472
♪

04:52.473 --> 04:54.508
- Brian, wait.
- Oh, hey, Carol.

04:54.509 --> 04:57.043
Do you need me to walk you to your car

04:57.044 --> 04:59.079
in case the studio audience guy
shows up?

04:59.080 --> 05:01.715
No, he killed himself
in my downstairs shower.

05:01.716 --> 05:03.583
Oh, good. That's good.

05:03.584 --> 05:06.753
I just wanted to thank you
for what you did today for Adam.

05:06.754 --> 05:08.421
He was a great man.

05:08.422 --> 05:10.557
You know, I see a lot of him in you.

05:10.558 --> 05:12.392
Oh, no. Are we gonna kiss?

05:12.393 --> 05:14.728
- We're gonna kiss, aren't we?
- I came here to say

05:14.729 --> 05:16.830
that what you did was very honorable.

05:16.831 --> 05:18.331
It showed real leadership,

05:18.332 --> 05:21.201
<i>and I think you should be
the next mayor of Quahog.</i>

05:21.202 --> 05:22.602
Ah, damn it!

05:22.603 --> 05:23.770
Oh, I couldn't do that.

05:23.771 --> 05:25.639
I don't know anything about politics.

05:25.640 --> 05:27.974
Although crazier things have happened.

05:27.975 --> 05:30.243
Harry Truman didn't have any experience.

05:30.244 --> 05:32.078
Of course he did. He was vice president,

05:32.079 --> 05:34.681
and before that,
a United States senator.

05:34.682 --> 05:35.949
Oh, word?

05:37.084 --> 05:39.786
Brian, is this gonna be
a politics episode?

05:39.787 --> 05:41.554
I-I think it might be.

05:49.630 --> 05:51.806
No one likes those.

05:56.003 --> 05:59.005
So, Carol was just going on and
on about how I should be mayor.

05:59.006 --> 06:01.875
<i>And it's got me thinking,
it is an interesting idea.</i>

06:01.876 --> 06:04.077
- You think I should do it?
- Absolutely not.

06:04.078 --> 06:06.079
- I mean, if not me, who?
- Anyone.

06:06.080 --> 06:07.681
- If not now, when?
- Never.

06:07.682 --> 06:09.783
<i>- You know, why not me?
- A million reasons.</i>

06:09.784 --> 06:11.178
I mean, who do you want in there,

06:11.179 --> 06:12.788
- some career politician?
- Yes.

06:12.789 --> 06:14.599
<i>- What are they gonna do?
- Govern.</i>

06:14.600 --> 06:16.122
Thanks, Stewie.
Your support means a lot.

06:16.123 --> 06:18.758
- You don't have it.
- You know what? I'm gonna do it.

06:18.759 --> 06:20.760
Guys, I have an announcement.

06:20.761 --> 06:24.097
- I'm gonna run for mayor.
- That's a terrible idea.

06:24.098 --> 06:26.666
You idiot, Brian. Meg, fart on Brian.

06:26.667 --> 06:29.102
I can't.
I don't have one in the chamber.

06:29.103 --> 06:31.938
The one time I give you
a chance, you're not ready.

06:31.939 --> 06:33.907
Chris, tag him for Meg.

06:36.544 --> 06:38.011
See that kid? He's a gamer.

06:38.012 --> 06:40.680
Great job, Chris.
Now, go hit the showers.

06:40.681 --> 06:43.416
Meg, you miss 100%
of the farts you don't take.

06:43.417 --> 06:46.186
That kid's going places.
He's going all the way.

06:49.890 --> 06:52.058
If only they knew.

06:59.870 --> 07:01.702
That's my boy!

07:08.290 --> 07:10.344
Welcome back, Quahog. And now it's time

07:10.345 --> 07:13.581
for a new segment on our show
called "On the Same Sofa,"

07:13.582 --> 07:15.916
in which a guest and I
have a conversation

07:15.917 --> 07:17.718
while sitting on the same sofa.

07:17.719 --> 07:20.588
My guest tonight is mayoral
candidate Brian Griffin.

07:20.589 --> 07:22.923
- Thank you for coming, Brian.
- Pleasure, Tom.

07:22.924 --> 07:25.259
And thank you for allowing me
up on the furniture.

07:25.260 --> 07:27.761
- I don't always get to do that.
- Oh, word?

07:27.762 --> 07:30.196
Now, I understand
you're running unopposed.

07:30.197 --> 07:32.665
That gives you a bit
of an advantage, doesn't it?

07:32.666 --> 07:34.901
Well, Tom, I welcome a challenger.

07:34.902 --> 07:37.504
Not the one that exploded, but, um...

07:37.505 --> 07:40.140
That's probably gonna get me
in trouble right there.

07:40.141 --> 07:41.801
Good thing I'm running unopposed.

07:41.802 --> 07:44.344
Well, we've now reached
the middle of the interview,

07:44.345 --> 07:46.813
where I ask the guest,
"How's the sofa so far?"

07:46.814 --> 07:48.675
So, Brian, how's the sofa so far?

07:48.676 --> 07:50.250
So far, so-so.

07:50.251 --> 07:51.518
I see. Sophie?

07:51.519 --> 07:53.106
So far we've got a so-so sofa.

07:53.107 --> 07:55.855
Great. Okay, Tom, we go live in three,

07:55.856 --> 07:58.244
- two...
- What? None of that aired?

07:58.245 --> 07:59.893
It's all right, we can recreate it.

07:59.894 --> 08:01.227
And you're on.

08:01.228 --> 08:03.897
So, Brian, I understand
you like eating your own poop.

08:03.898 --> 08:05.261
<i>What's that about?</i>

08:05.262 --> 08:06.596
Argh. Turn that off.

08:06.597 --> 08:08.664
I can't believe we're
gonna have a dog for mayor.

08:08.665 --> 08:10.833
We're gonna be the laughingstock
of the whole country.

08:10.834 --> 08:12.702
Even Sean Hannity's talking about us.

08:12.703 --> 08:14.237
He's a weird-looking guy.

08:14.238 --> 08:16.839
- Put up a picture of Sean Hannity.
- Can we do that?

08:16.840 --> 08:19.242
Yeah, Tosh does it
all the time. Put it up.

08:19.243 --> 08:20.576
Yeah, he does look weird.

08:20.577 --> 08:22.178
Yeah. Who does he look like?

08:22.179 --> 08:24.013
I'm seeing Mr. Doubtfire.

08:24.014 --> 08:25.715
High-sodium Superman?

08:25.716 --> 08:28.460
He looks like an angry
face drawn on a thumb.

08:28.461 --> 08:30.062
The richest guy at Rite Aid?

08:30.063 --> 08:31.830
Or the mayor who won't close

08:31.831 --> 08:33.298
<i>the beaches in Jaws.</i>

08:33.299 --> 08:35.067
Wreck-It Ralph at a job interview.

08:35.068 --> 08:36.435
You know that's a guy

08:36.436 --> 08:38.937
who's roughly led his wife
out of parties by the elbow.

08:38.938 --> 08:41.306
A guy whose ice cream
parlor just went broke.

08:41.307 --> 08:43.008
He looks like a handsome Weeble.

08:43.009 --> 08:44.643
Or a hot Frankenstein.

08:44.644 --> 08:46.778
Yeah, but either way,
he's that Little League coach

08:46.779 --> 08:48.580
the parents hope their kids don't get.

08:48.581 --> 08:51.416
He looks like a fish that
inflates to scare predators.

08:51.417 --> 08:53.418
The inside trader who kills himself

08:53.419 --> 08:55.754
the day his prison
sentence is supposed to start.

08:55.755 --> 08:57.856
I'm thinking Fred and Barney's son.

08:57.857 --> 09:00.225
Trust me on this.
Strip club lunch regular.

09:00.226 --> 09:01.793
I feel like that's a dad

09:01.794 --> 09:03.662
who's ripped his kid's posters
off the wall.

09:03.663 --> 09:06.131
And sleeps in
pajamas buttoned to the top.

09:06.132 --> 09:08.600
72-ounce steak contest entrant.

09:08.601 --> 09:11.570
Drowned-in-the-lake-
last-month Colin Farrell.

09:11.571 --> 09:12.771
All right, that was fun.

09:12.772 --> 09:15.007
Hey, let's do Matthew Perry. I'll start.

09:15.008 --> 09:16.375
He looks like a pelican

09:16.376 --> 09:18.377
trying to swallow a fish that's too big.

09:18.378 --> 09:20.379
Barn owl in human skin.

09:20.380 --> 09:22.381
He looks like he told a genie

09:22.382 --> 09:25.150
- he wished to be a pool noodle.
- Hey, guys?

09:25.151 --> 09:28.449
<i>Friends brings me a lot of joy,
so can we stop this?</i>

09:39.465 --> 09:40.999
Hail to the dog

09:41.000 --> 09:43.502
Every tree in town is mine now

09:43.503 --> 09:45.337
Open the window

09:45.338 --> 09:47.172
I'm gonna bite the air.

10:03.456 --> 10:05.057
What's this?

10:05.058 --> 10:07.693
Well, looks like stolen property
and vandalism, for starters.

10:07.694 --> 10:10.262
Uh, can you hang on?
I'm finishing a phone interview.

10:10.263 --> 10:12.097
And that's why I would never joke

10:12.098 --> 10:14.166
<i>about the Space Shuttle
Challenger tragedy.</i>

10:14.167 --> 10:16.134
I can't believe I said that twice.

10:16.135 --> 10:17.669
Now, how can I help you, Brian?

10:17.670 --> 10:20.038
Why are you doing this?
Why are you running for mayor?

10:20.039 --> 10:22.162
Uh, let me think.
Oh, yeah. Out of spite.

10:22.163 --> 10:23.485
Spite for you.

10:23.486 --> 10:25.210
That's not a reason
to get into politics.

10:25.211 --> 10:27.579
It's the only reason
to get into politics.

10:27.580 --> 10:29.982
Well, you're just wasting your time,
because you're not gonna win.

10:29.983 --> 10:31.149
I don't know about that.

10:31.150 --> 10:32.551
You seem pretty afraid.

10:32.552 --> 10:34.252
The only thing I'm afraid of

10:34.253 --> 10:36.622
are fire truck sirens
and things that look like faces.

10:36.623 --> 10:38.268
Fine. See you at the debate.

10:38.269 --> 10:40.058
Fine!

10:40.059 --> 10:41.727
- What are you gonna wear?
- I don't know.

10:41.728 --> 10:44.129
I was thinking, like, a
collared shirt, jacket, no tie.

10:44.130 --> 10:46.932
- Yeah, yeah, no tie.
- Yeah, definitely no tie.

10:49.769 --> 10:51.937
That son of a bitch.

10:51.938 --> 10:53.805
Good evening.
I'm Tom Tucker, and I will be

10:53.806 --> 10:55.440
your moderator
for tonight's mayoral debate.

10:55.441 --> 10:57.843
Not because I want to,
but because it counts

10:57.844 --> 10:59.945
as community service
for open-hand smacking

10:59.946 --> 11:01.346
an Uber Eats guy.

11:01.347 --> 11:02.881
Let's meet our candidates.

11:02.882 --> 11:05.569
First, the impeccably-dressed
Glenn Quagmire.

11:05.570 --> 11:07.828
- Thank you, Tom.
- Is that a Windsor knot?

11:07.829 --> 11:09.106
Double Windsor, Tom.

11:09.107 --> 11:10.756
Excellent. Some might describe

11:10.757 --> 11:12.924
that tie as "mayoral."

11:12.925 --> 11:15.661
Next up, we have
super-caj Brian Griffin.

11:15.662 --> 11:17.897
I was gonna wear a tie.
He told me not to.

11:17.898 --> 11:20.299
He's already losing,
and it hasn't started yet.

11:20.300 --> 11:22.501
First question: as candidates for mayor,

11:22.502 --> 11:24.704
how do I put my apps into a folder?

11:24.705 --> 11:26.172
I know how to get them shaky,

11:26.173 --> 11:27.873
I just can't get them in a folder.

11:27.874 --> 11:29.208
You just drag them into each other.

11:29.209 --> 11:30.610
But you know what else is shaky?

11:30.611 --> 11:32.511
My opponent's economic plan.

11:32.512 --> 11:35.314
It's irresponsible for the town
to get two credit cards

11:35.315 --> 11:37.750
and just swap the balance
back and forth each month.

11:37.751 --> 11:40.119
But-but the town would get miles.

11:40.120 --> 11:42.890
Whoa, so I can just name
the folder whatever I want?

11:42.891 --> 11:44.885
"Tom's Stuff."

11:44.886 --> 11:47.827
Okay, Tom, we go live in three, two...

11:47.828 --> 11:51.163
Good evening, Quahog, and
welcome to your mayoral debate.

11:51.164 --> 11:54.133
What the... None of that aired?
I was totally winning.

11:54.134 --> 11:55.401
That's okay, we'll recreate it.

11:55.402 --> 11:58.137
Now, Mr. Quagmire,
you're a dirty sex fiend.

11:58.138 --> 12:01.107
Why would you wear a tie
to a casual debate?

12:01.108 --> 12:02.375
Good question, Tom.

12:02.376 --> 12:05.911
And I'll answer that
with one word: pizza!

12:07.748 --> 12:09.715
Damn it, he burned me twice.

12:09.716 --> 12:12.118
And, you're not gonna, like,
bring pizza for everyone, right?

12:12.119 --> 12:13.953
No, it's a debate.
They'll have food there.

12:13.954 --> 12:16.255
Right, they' have food there.
Okay, so, no tie, no pizza.

12:16.256 --> 12:18.324
I'll see you there.

12:21.028 --> 12:22.962
Open the door, Quagmire.

12:22.963 --> 12:26.280
Hey, Brian. I was just
emptying my bus garbage.

12:26.281 --> 12:27.667
Would you like to eat it first?

12:27.668 --> 12:29.535
What's the catch?

12:29.536 --> 12:31.297
God, you're a dumb beast.

12:31.298 --> 12:32.872
Come on in.

12:40.947 --> 12:44.216
- Have a seat, Brian.
- I'm fine standing, thank you.

12:44.217 --> 12:46.319
Let's cut the crap. The only
reason you're running is...

12:46.320 --> 12:48.654
to make me look ridiculous.

12:48.655 --> 12:50.189
And I am not just some idiot

12:50.190 --> 12:52.925
to be laughed at
and not taken seriously.

12:52.926 --> 12:54.860
Ha! Sit down, Snoopy.

12:54.861 --> 12:57.163
What did you say?

12:57.164 --> 13:01.901
I said, "Sit, Ubu, sit. Good dog."

13:01.902 --> 13:03.636
You son of a bitch!

13:05.906 --> 13:09.075
You idiot! He's allergic
to getting hit in the head!

13:09.076 --> 13:10.943
♪

13:27.527 --> 13:29.528
♪

13:41.691 --> 13:43.358
Oh, my God, we're gonna die!

13:43.359 --> 13:45.594
Calm down, Brian. This bus has OnStar.

13:45.595 --> 13:47.596
<i>OnStar roadside assistance.</i>

13:47.597 --> 13:50.099
Yes, our bus went over a cliff.
We need help.

13:50.100 --> 13:51.467
<i>Glenn?</i>

13:51.468 --> 13:53.836
<i>I-Is this Glenn Quagmire?</i>

13:53.837 --> 13:55.504
Yes, sweetheart. Hi, who's this?

13:55.505 --> 13:58.956
<i>It's Melissa. From the Ramada Inn.</i>

13:58.957 --> 14:00.008
Oh.

14:00.009 --> 14:03.378
The Framingham Ramada Inn
or the Cranston Ramada Inn?

14:03.379 --> 14:04.913
<i>Cranston.</i>

14:04.914 --> 14:06.448
Oh, yeah, we're gonna die.

14:14.971 --> 14:17.139
I think my leg is broken.

14:17.140 --> 14:20.008
Oh, my God, how are we gonna
get down from here?

14:21.077 --> 14:23.145
- You think he's dead?
- I don't know.

14:23.146 --> 14:25.301
Hey. Hey, buddy?

14:26.482 --> 14:29.618
- What's his name?
- Uh, it's something Spanishy.

14:29.619 --> 14:31.620
I-I think it starts with a "G"?

14:31.621 --> 14:34.356
G-Gerr, G-Ga, Goo...

14:34.357 --> 14:37.592
Goo, Goo-gar... Goo-gardo.
G... Yeah, that's it, Googardo.

14:37.593 --> 14:38.994
That doesn't sound like any name.

14:38.995 --> 14:40.629
Well, sure it does. Googardo?

14:40.630 --> 14:42.464
Say something if you're okay, Googardo.

14:42.465 --> 14:44.966
The more you say it, the more
it doesn't sound like anything.

14:44.967 --> 14:48.417
Googardo? Move something
if you're alive, Googardo.

14:55.511 --> 14:58.380
- Oh, my God!
- Oh, look, there's his jacket.

14:58.381 --> 15:00.215
Oh, yeah, his name was Frank.

15:00.216 --> 15:03.585
I can't believe this. I'm gonna
die with Glenn Quagmire.

15:03.586 --> 15:06.454
Hey, dying with Glenn Quagmire
was good enough for Googardo.

15:06.455 --> 15:08.623
<i>Vaya con Dios, Googy.</i>

15:08.624 --> 15:10.292
Please don't use the familiar form

15:10.293 --> 15:12.561
of a guy's name you never knew.

15:16.732 --> 15:19.034
What was I thinking getting
on this bus with you?

15:19.035 --> 15:22.304
It was dumber than when Peter
hired that raccoon accountant.

15:22.305 --> 15:23.939
All right, well, you're the money guy.

15:23.940 --> 15:27.482
Let's put it all in
to slightly-open trash cans.

15:35.551 --> 15:37.219
You have anything to eat in here?

15:37.220 --> 15:38.553
Yeah, there's some edible underwear

15:38.554 --> 15:39.721
in that bag over there.

15:39.722 --> 15:41.256
Ugh, isn't there anything else?

15:41.257 --> 15:43.892
I have a ball of peanut butter
with a pill inside.

15:43.893 --> 15:46.676
Hmm, wish you hadn't told me
about the pill.

15:55.170 --> 15:57.568
You know, this underwear's not bad.

15:57.569 --> 15:59.541
Are they for your political groupies?

15:59.542 --> 16:00.875
No, these-these are men's.

16:00.876 --> 16:02.344
They're-they're mine.

16:04.480 --> 16:07.682
Quagmire, why did you
even want to be mayor?

16:07.683 --> 16:10.619
Honestly? I just want
a street named after me.

16:10.620 --> 16:12.187
I think that's kind of cool.

16:12.188 --> 16:14.055
<i>Actually, that is kind of cool.</i>

16:14.056 --> 16:15.557
Why did you want to be mayor?

16:15.558 --> 16:19.461
Mayor West told me he went
to 65 pancake breakfasts a year.

16:19.462 --> 16:22.467
That number... That-that stuck with mat

16:22.468 --> 16:24.799
What, like, the...
like, the pancakes were free?

16:24.800 --> 16:27.269
- Yeah.
- 65.

16:27.270 --> 16:29.537
That-That's, like, pancakes
every Saturday morning

16:29.538 --> 16:30.872
and probably some Sundays.

16:30.873 --> 16:33.108
And sometimes it's, like,
kids making the pancakes,

16:33.109 --> 16:34.876
and-and you get these mondo huge ones.

16:34.877 --> 16:36.578
Wow.

16:36.579 --> 16:38.747
Probably no
chocolate chip pancakes, though.

16:38.748 --> 16:41.082
Are you kidding me?
65 a year, you're gonna get

16:41.083 --> 16:43.418
at least eight to ten
chocolate chip pancake events.

16:43.419 --> 16:45.186
- You think eight to ten?
- Yes.

16:45.187 --> 16:47.889
And now that I say it out loud,
eight to ten sounds low.

16:47.890 --> 16:50.392
So, pancakes is why
you wanted to be mayor?

16:50.393 --> 16:53.762
Well, pancakes and...
look at the people in our town.

16:53.763 --> 16:55.730
- Who else is gonna do it?
- I know.

16:55.731 --> 16:57.666
This is such a garbage town.

16:57.667 --> 16:59.701
You know, when you think about it,

16:59.702 --> 17:02.103
we're really
the only two viable candidates.

17:02.104 --> 17:03.538
I mean, you're a pilot.

17:03.539 --> 17:05.473
You're responsible for people's lives.

17:05.474 --> 17:06.808
You make quick decisions.

17:06.809 --> 17:09.577
Or the machinery in the plane
makes quick decisions.

17:09.578 --> 17:11.513
M-My point is, you're a smart guy.

17:11.514 --> 17:13.515
Thank you.

17:13.516 --> 17:16.284
And now you say something nice about me.

17:16.285 --> 17:19.187
- Like what?
- Like I'm good company,

17:19.188 --> 17:20.555
and I'm smart and funny,

17:20.556 --> 17:22.624
and I'm invited
to all your pool parties.

17:22.625 --> 17:25.794
And I should just come over
if I hear one of them going on.

17:25.795 --> 17:27.162
No, thank you.

17:27.163 --> 17:28.797
But... but you have to.

17:28.798 --> 17:30.432
I'm not gonna say something I don't mean

17:30.433 --> 17:32.167
just because your ego needs to hear it.

17:32.168 --> 17:34.502
See? That's why I ran against you.

17:34.503 --> 17:36.871
Because I know that's the only
reason you were doing this.

17:36.872 --> 17:38.773
You're a complete tool!

17:38.774 --> 17:40.442
<i>You do sound like kind of a tool.</i>

17:40.443 --> 17:43.345
See? Even Melissa from OnStar
thinks you're a tool.

17:43.346 --> 17:45.080
You've been listening this whole time?

17:45.081 --> 17:47.182
<i>There's nothing to do at OnStar.</i>

17:47.183 --> 17:48.550
<i>People have iPhones now.</i>

17:48.551 --> 17:51.453
<i>I just listen in to cars.
Sometimes there's sex.</i>

17:51.454 --> 17:53.922
Screw this. We just got
to get out of this bus.

17:53.923 --> 17:56.024
Regardless of what we think
of each other,

17:56.025 --> 17:57.792
this is no way for us to die.

17:57.793 --> 17:59.494
I'm gonna try and climb up to the street

17:59.495 --> 18:01.663
- and see if I can get help.
- Just be careful.

18:01.664 --> 18:03.598
I don't know how stable this thing is.

18:12.508 --> 18:14.642
Oh, my God.
You just got hit in the throat

18:14.643 --> 18:16.010
with a gentleman's dildo.

18:16.011 --> 18:18.046
<i>- Hey, Melissa.
- What? What happened?</i>

18:18.047 --> 18:20.849
He got hit in the throat
with a gentleman's dildo.

18:20.850 --> 18:23.017
<i>See,</i>

18:23.018 --> 18:24.886
<i>this is why I listen.</i>

18:26.522 --> 18:28.923
♪

18:56.919 --> 18:59.587
♪

18:59.588 --> 19:01.189
Mayor West?

19:19.041 --> 19:20.642
Hey, guys. Don't mind me.

19:20.643 --> 19:23.344
I'm gonna go steal
that bus driver's identity.

19:23.345 --> 19:26.081
The Celtics are free money tonight!

19:32.022 --> 19:34.757
Well, Lois, you almost had
a female president.

19:34.758 --> 19:36.259
I almost had a dog mayor.

19:36.260 --> 19:38.161
I can't believe
they canceled the election

19:38.162 --> 19:40.863
after they thought Brian
and Mr. Quagmire were dead.

19:40.864 --> 19:43.199
Does that mean we still need a mayor?

19:43.200 --> 19:44.801
<i>It sure does, America.</i>

19:44.802 --> 19:47.370
<i>Who do you think should be
the next mayor of Quahog.</i>

19:47.371 --> 19:50.540
<i>Register your votes
at fox.com/family-guy.</i>

19:50.541 --> 19:52.208
Your votes don't count. It's a trick.

19:52.209 --> 19:55.411
<i>- They're just tracking your data.
- No, it's not. No, it's not.</i>

19:55.412 --> 19:58.047
Is Mr. Quagmire okay after the accident?

19:58.048 --> 20:01.551
Yeah, he's fine. He's having one
of his private pool parties.

20:04.688 --> 20:06.289
Hey, girls. Thanks for coming.

20:06.290 --> 20:08.858
Is your voice still broken
from the accident?

20:08.859 --> 20:10.526
No, no, I-I'm just trying to be quiet.

20:10.527 --> 20:11.894
Grab yourself a drink.

20:11.895 --> 20:13.696
I'm gonna have some chips first.

20:13.697 --> 20:15.031
No, no, no!

20:15.032 --> 20:18.067
Is that a pool party I hear?

20:19.103 --> 20:21.270
Cannonball!

20:21.271 --> 20:23.840
<i>And that was the moment I remembered...</i>

20:23.841 --> 20:25.875
<i>Quagmire doesn't have a swimming pool.</i>

20:33.584 --> 20:35.451
<i>I want to be a mayor</i>

20:35.452 --> 20:37.120
in real life.

20:37.121 --> 20:38.921
So I'm here to ask you

20:38.922 --> 20:41.157
to make me the mayor of your town.

20:41.158 --> 20:43.159
Vote for me, Adam West.

20:43.160 --> 20:46.729
It'll be a home run.

20:46.730 --> 20:48.731
Ugh.

20:52.069 --> 20:54.570
It'll be a home run.

20:55.572 --> 20:57.607
Pow!

21:00.936 --> 21:04.936
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv